<tr id="A6.T11.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T11.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;"><span id="A6.T11.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ScienceWorld</span></td>
<td id="A6.T11.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">90</td>
<td id="A6.T11.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">
<span id="A6.T11.2.3.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block">
<span id="A6.T11.2.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_block ltx_parbox ltx_align_middle" style="width:345.0pt;">
<span id="A6.T11.2.3.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.T11.2.3.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Task:</span> <em id="A6.T11.2.3.3.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Find the animal with the longest life span.</em></span>
<span id="A6.T11.2.3.3.1.1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<span id="A6.T11.2.3.3.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="A6.T11.2.3.3.1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">
<span id="A6.T11.2.3.3.1.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:2.0pt;">
<span id="A6.T11.2.3.3.1.1.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="A6.T11.2.3.3.1.1.2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">T:</span></span>
</span></span>
<span id="A6.T11.2.3.3.1.1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding-top:0.75pt;padding-bottom:0.75pt;">
<span id="A6.T11.2.3.3.1.1.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:325.0pt;">
<span id="A6.T11.2.3.3.1.1.2.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left">I need to focus on the animal with the longest lifespan. Since the bee hive is open and contains multiple adult bees, I should focus on the bees first.</span>
</span></span></span>
